       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem, and I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note.\n\n6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum recommended daily dose of 3,200 mg. I'm not aware of any standard indication for it. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below this dose, but the GI bleeding, kidney, and cardiovascular risks keep rising. An order like this should go through a check that I can't do from here.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily right away, or another dose you choose.\n- **Use your hospital's high-dose override process.** This usually means pharmacist review and direct documentation from the specialist, such as a consult note with the dose and rationale. The order may need to be entered by the prescriber or through a different workflow.\n- **Ask the specialist about alternatives.** If standard dosing failed, another NSAID or a different drug class may fit better than exceeding the ibuprofen maximum.\n\nIf you want me to enter one of the within-limit doses, tell me which."
      }
